<article class="env-example" id="0089">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0089">Example <span data-tag="0089">2.2.7.4</span>.</a> Let $G$ be a group with identity element $1 \in G$, let $\Gamma $ be an abelian group on which $G$ acts by automorphisms, let $\alpha : G \times G \times G \rightarrow \Gamma $ be a $3$-cocycle, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be the monoidal category of Example <a data-tag="00CS" href="/tag/00CS">2.1.3.3</a>, and let $B\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be the bicategory obtained by delooping $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (Example <a data-tag="00F1" href="/tag/00F1">2.2.2.5</a>). The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The $3$-cocycle $\alpha $ is <em>normalized</em>: that is, it satisfies the equations 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \alpha _{x,y,1} = \alpha _{x,1,y} = \alpha _{1,x,y} = 0 \]
</div>
<p>
 for every pair of elements $x,y \in G$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The bicategory $B\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is strictly unital, in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="00FD" href="/tag/00FD">2.2.7.1</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
